-- ====================================================================
-- Vendor Evaluation v2 — Consolidated Business Data Seed (02 of 3)
--
-- Apply AFTER vendor_eval_v2_01_schema.sql and BEFORE
-- vendor_eval_v2_03_seed_requestor_contacts.sql.
--
-- Combines two seed exports generated 2026-07-06 from local DB
-- u894129685_workspace (KLG-PROC-I01271, MariaDB 10.4.32), both generated
-- programmatically from live rows (not hand-typed):
--
--   SECTION A — Question-set seed (11 active sets, 65 active questions,
--               11 active taxonomy maps). Includes question_section /
--               input_type (identification vs evaluation questions).
--   SECTION B — PO taxonomy seed (311 rows, status='mapped' only —
--               excludes 41 local 'needs_review' rows, which are
--               unconfirmed and better re-reviewed fresh on the target).
--
-- >>> master_data_id CAVEAT <<<
-- The master_data_id-based refresh (tools/refresh_vendor_eval_po_taxonomy_
-- from_master_data.php) was evaluated but NOT applied to this seed: local
-- prs.master_data_id has zero populated rows (see
-- db_backups/vendor_eval_v2_deployment_handover.txt), so Section B below
-- is still sourced from the fuzzy item-description matcher
-- (tools/run_po_taxonomy_mapping.php), not from master_data_id. Once a
-- target has real prs.master_data_id data (production, after main is
-- reconciled), prefer regenerating Section B's data with the refresh tool
-- over importing this section as-is.
--
-- >>> PO taxonomy IMPORTANT CAVEAT <<<
-- vendor_eval_po_taxonomy rows are DERIVED data: each row is only
-- meaningful if the target's own `prs` table contains the SAME po_number.
-- There is no FK enforcing this. RECOMMENDED PATH on any target with its
-- own live `prs` data (real production): run
-- tools/run_po_taxonomy_mapping.php (dry-run first) directly against that
-- target instead of importing Section B — that regenerates correct,
-- current mappings for whatever POs actually exist there. Section B is
-- only a fallback for environments cloning the same PO population (e.g. QA).
--
-- No requestor contact PII, no public_token anywhere in this file.
--
-- Idempotent / re-runnable: question sets keyed on (set_code, version);
-- questions on (question_set_id, question_no); taxonomy maps on
-- (map_level, taxonomy_level_2, taxonomy_level_3); PO taxonomy on
-- (po_number). Re-running updates existing rows in place.
--
-- Apply with (after verifying identity):
--   mysql -h HOST -u USER -p DATABASE < db_backups/vendor_eval_v2_02_seed_business_data.sql
-- ====================================================================


